# 🎲 Pig Game

A fun, turn-based dice game for two players, built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript .

![Pig Game Screenshot](screenshot.png)

- **Source Code:** [GitHub Repository](https://github.com/m3tazbaha01-collab/Pig-game.git)

## 📖 About the Project

Pig Game is a two-player dice game where players take turns rolling a die to accumulate points. Players must decide when to keep rolling and when to hold their score to avoid losing their current points.

This project was completed as a learning exercise inspired by Jonas Schmedtmann's JavaScript course on Udemy.

## 🎮 How to Play

1. Click **Roll Dice** to roll the die.
2. The rolled number is added to your current score.
3. Click **Hold** to save your current score and pass the turn to the other player.
4. Rolling a **1** resets your current score and ends your turn.
5. The first player to reach **100 points** wins the game.
6. Click **New Game** to start over.

## ✨ Features

- Two-player turn-based gameplay
- Random dice rolls
- Current and total score tracking
- Hold and turn-switching mechanics
- Winning condition and game reset
- Interactive user interface

## 🛠️ Built With

- **HTML5** — Page structure
- **CSS3** — Styling and layout
- **JavaScript** — Game logic, DOM manipulation, and event handling

## 💡 Work by

- Selecting and manipulating DOM elements
- Handling user interactions with event listeners
- Managing game state and player turns
- Working with conditional logic and random numbers
- Updating the interface dynamically with JavaScript

